# n8n.env -- n8n encryption-key config, machine-local, NEVER committed.
#
# Real location: ~/.local/share/n8n/n8n.env (gitignored; beside the n8n
# sqlite DB it configures, mirroring kb.env living beside the KB). From
# this repo's root, copy this file there and edit it:
#
#   cp scripts/n8n-container/n8n.env.example ~/.local/share/n8n/n8n.env
#   chmod 600 ~/.local/share/n8n/n8n.env
#
# n8n-secret.py resolve-secret reads this file and prints exactly one
# `N8N_ENCRYPTION_KEY=<value>` line for the quadlet's ExecStartPre to write
# to a tmpfs EnvironmentFile. The value is never logged.

# --- N8N_ENCRYPTION_KEY: REQUIRED, and must PERSIST across restarts ------
#
# This key encrypts stored credentials inside n8n's own sqlite DB. Losing
# or changing it ORPHANS every credential already stored in n8n. Generate
# it ONCE (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`) and never rotate it casually.
#
# Pick ONE of the two modes below.
#
# Mode 1: static value (simplest, least secure -- sits in this file).
# N8N_ENCRYPTION_KEY=REPLACE_ME   (value from: openssl rand -hex 32)
#
# Mode 2: vault command (preferred). n8n-secret.py runs this exact command
# and uses its stdout as the key; wins over N8N_ENCRYPTION_KEY if both are
# set. Works with any vault CLI. For Proton Pass, see
# ~/.claude/skills/proton-pass-cli/SKILL.md for the pass-cli invocation and
# its PROTON_PASS_SESSION_DIR / PROTON_PASS_AGENT_REASON requirements. The
# key is stored as the `password` field of a MachineSecrets login item
# titled `n8n-encryption-key`:
# N8N_ENCRYPTION_KEY_CMD="pass-cli item view --vault-name MachineSecrets --item-title n8n-encryption-key --field password"

# --- N8N_API_KEY: OPTIONAL, only needed for agent-driven create/trigger --
#
# Authenticates calls to n8n's Public REST API (X-N8N-API-KEY header).
# Unlike the encryption key, a missing API key does NOT break n8n itself
# -- it's only needed if an agent wants to create/list/activate workflows
# via the API. There is no headless mint path in n8n Community
# edition: a human must log into the n8n editor once (http://127.0.0.1:5678)
# and go to Settings -> n8n API -> Create an API Key, then store the value
# here (or in the vault, Mode 2 below).
#
# Pick ONE of the two modes below.
#
# Mode 1: static value (simplest, least secure -- sits in this file).
# N8N_API_KEY=REPLACE_ME   (create in n8n editor: Settings, n8n API)
#
# Mode 2: vault command (preferred). n8n-secret.py runs this exact command
# and uses its stdout as the key; wins over N8N_API_KEY if both are set.
# The key is stored as the `api-key` field of a MachineSecrets login item
# titled `n8n-api-key`:
# N8N_API_KEY_CMD="pass-cli item view --vault-name MachineSecrets --item-title n8n-api-key --field api-key"
